 "notes": "Section 8 (South of Market, Mission Bay and the waterfront piers; Bay of San Francisco on the right as scanned; joins Sec. 1 above, 7 left, 9 lower left), 1-bit photocopy, 5400x4127, the sheet lies on its side (title reads top to bottom). Page turned ~0.2 deg (top rule y 363 at the left to 348 at the right; left rule x 284 at the top to 295 at the bottom). Frame on all four sides: thick bar, ~4-5 px of white, thin inner rule (4-5 px, the innermost rule), with a thick + thin quarter arc (radius ~201-213 px) in every corner. The outline lies on paper 1-2 px inside the thin rule's inner edge, or on the first clean paper row beside it where the rule's edge is ragged (README rules 1, 8), points every <=60 px. Corners (rule 2): the outline follows the inner edge of the thin arc 1-2 px inside it; each thin arc's tail runs beside its side rule and joins it through a short connector, and the outline goes round tail and connector (TL: connector on the left rule at y 577-582 and on the top rule at x 501-506; TR: x 4879-4884 and y 564-568; BL: y 3734-3738 and x 512-515; BR: y 3728-3732 and x 4880-4885). TL corner: solid commercial and cross-hatched blocks run across the thin arc for most of its length; its inner edge is the circle about the centre of the cleanly printed thick arc (502.2,580.8), radius 206.5, checked where streets cross the arc (thin arc ~6 px wide, ~5 px inside the thick one), and the outline follows it through the block ink; the block parts beyond the arc are outside (rule 2). Kind (b), map ink that truly touches the frame and is left under the outline: along the top the solid commercial blocks of the Market Street strip run into the thin rule for most of its length (x ~520-4150), so the outline follows the rule's inner edge (fitted from the street openings between the blocks, ~50% of the side) through fully black stretches: this is most of the ink under the outline; on the left the cross-hatched industrial blocks and street lines run into the left rule (y ~640-2530); a street line meets the TL connector on the top rule (x 504-509) and is crossed there. The right and bottom sides face open bay and blank paper. 'Join Sec. 9' is lettered inside the frame in the blank lower-left triangle and stays map (README rule 4: cross-references are inside); BAY OF SAN FRANCISCO and the PIER HEAD LINE lettering stay map. remove: (1) the rotated CITY & COUNTY OF SAN FRANCISCO / USE OF PROPERTY / ZONE MAP / CITY PLANNING COMMISSION title, LEGEND with its six swatches, and the SCALE bar with its lettering (lower right, no ruled box, on open bay paper), a rectangle 5.5 px outside its ink (ink x 4199-4852, y 2784-3466); (2) the compass rose with its two long arrows (tips 4066,2869 and 4134,2962) and the tail feather (3471-3526, 3412-3464): it stands in the open bay and overlaps no map ink, but the dash-dot PIER HEAD LINE and its lettering pass 15-30 px from its west side (HEAD is ~17 px from the west ray), so the 13-point outline keeps 6-10 px outside the compass ink and leaves the line and the lettering as map; (3) the SECTION 8 badge (ring centre 4981.4,3795.1, outer radius 57.9), an octagon 5 px outside the ring, on open paper. Doubt: the TL arc, where block ink hides the thin arc's inner edge for long stretches (read from the fitted circle).",
